body:
Thank you, @raulsntos, this is very helpful. 🙏 I think Godot could potentially make _something_ clearer here—and I'll talk about that below—but I'd like to shed some light on what led to this issue:

- I was profiling my C# code.
- I saw `Godot.NativeInterop.NativeFuncs.godotsharp_string_new_with_utf16_chars` and `Godot.NativeInterop.Marshaling.ConvertStringToNative` taking up 4.4% of my execution time.
- I hadn't been aware of this behavior and ended up finding [this documentation page](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.html#current-gotchas-and-known-issues).

This prompted two things:

- I assumed _all_ well-known `StringName`s would be exposed by Godot (hence the creation of this issue).
- I ditched C# strings everywhere in my code and manifested my own static class to track every `StringName`:

<details>
<summary>Large-ish static class definition</summary>

```cs
public static class GodotStringNames
{
    public static readonly StringName FontColor = "font_color";
    public static readonly StringName NormalFontSize = "normal_font_size";
    // [...] omitted for brevity - my actual file for this has 66 strings defined
    public static readonly StringName MarginTop = "margin_top";

    #region Shader parameters
    public static readonly StringName LineWidth = "line_width";
    // [...] omitted for brevity - my actual file for this has 66 strings defined
    public static readonly StringName LineColor = "line_color";
    #endregion

    #region Animation names
    public static readonly StringName Default = "default";
    #endregion

    #region Group names
    public static readonly StringName WanderRegion = "wander_region";
    #endregion

    #region Input names
    public static readonly StringName UiCancel = "ui_cancel";
    public static readonly StringName UiAccept = "ui_accept";
    // [...] omitted for brevity - my actual file for this has 66 strings defined
    public static readonly StringName UiZoomOut = "ui_zoom_out";
    #endregion
}
```
</details>

Some questions to determine future work:

- _Do_ we consider the lack of `StringName`s for themes to be an issue? I could see it going either way since it's trivial to define `static string`s ourselves.
- Do we want an update to the documentation to talk about custom-defined `StringName`s, e.g. for `SpriteFrames.SetAnimationSpeed`, `InputEvent.IsActionPressed`, etc.? I don't mind making a PR for this myself, but I'm not sure if my code snippet above is "overkill". E.g. I assume that almost _every_ Godot game using C# has some form of an `_Input` function calling some form of `InputEvent.IsActionPressed`, and hard-coding something like `InputEvent.IsActionPressed("ui_accept")` would cause unnecessary marshaling.

P.S. I think I saw `AddThemeFontSizeOverride` in the profiler, too, and I ended up changing my code after realizing that it wasn't performant, but I appreciate you pointing it out here.
